# 2. `packages/imessage/src/remote/reactions.ts` — the closest analogue

## Target resolution: cache hit → API fetch → rebuild → cache (`:58-85`)

```ts
const resolveReactionTarget = async (
  client: AdvancedIMessage,
  cache: MessageCache,
  chat: string,
  targetGuid: string,
  partIndex: number | undefined,
  phone: string
): Promise<IMessageMessage | undefined> => {
  let candidate = cache.get(targetGuid);
  if (!candidate) {
    try {
      const fetched = await client.messages.get(toMessageGuid(targetGuid));
      candidate = await rebuildFromAppleMessage(client, fetched, phone, chat);
      cacheMessage(cache, candidate);
    } catch {
      return;
    }
  }
  if (candidate.content.type === "group") {
    const items = candidate.content.items;
    if (!Array.isArray(items)) {
      return candidate;
    }
    const item = items[partIndex ?? 0];
    return isIMessageMessage(item) ? item : candidate;
  }
  return candidate;
};
```

Key behaviors to mirror for a read receipt: (a) bare `catch {}` — a failed fetch drops the event entirely rather than throwing (so `skipUnmappable` isn't even needed for that path); (b) `rebuildFromAppleMessage` sets `direction` from `message.isFromMe`, so a target that is *your* outbound message comes back `direction: "outbound"` (tested at `test/remote/reactions.test.ts:144-164`); (c) group parts are dereferenced by `partIndex`.

