2. **`docs/nav.json`** — insert `"spectrum-ts/content/read"` after `content/unsend` (groups with the fire-and-forget signals).
3. **`docs/providers/imessage/messaging-features.mdx.vel`** — new `## Inbound read receipts` section after `## Inbound group events` (`:145-179`), mirroring its table + `<Warning>` pattern. The warning covers volume: one event per participant per message, and because `chats.markRead` marks *every* unread message, one chat-open can produce a burst — make sure your loop's `default:` arm doesn't reply to them. "Semantics to rely on" bullets: sender always present; timestamp is read time; aggregate by `target.id`; the agent's own `space.read(...)` never echoes; a restart replays receipts and may drop ones whose target can no longer be resolved.
